"color: #333333; font-weight: 600; display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; gap: 20px;\" target=\"_blank\"> <svg class=\"download_svg\" fill=\"none\" height=\"65\" viewbox=\"0 0 65 65\" width=\"65\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"> <path d=\"M34.7087 0.802246L51.9921 16.7998V63.2344C51.9921 64.0948 51.2946 64.7922 50.4342 64.7922H2.24001C1.37961 64.7922 0.682129 64.0948 0.682129 63.2344V2.36012C0.682129 1.49973 1.37961 0.802246 2.24001 0.802246H34.7087Z\" fill=\"#2172D0\" fill-rule=\"evenodd\"></path> <path d=\"M2.89377 4.57204C2.89377 3.71164 3.59125 3.01416 4.45165 3.01416H33.4957C33.9151 3.01416 34.3168 3.18328 34.6099 3.48327L41.4271 10.46L49.2189 16.9423C49.5747 17.2383 49.7804 17.6771 49.7804 18.1399V61.023C49.7804 61.8834 49.083 62.5809 48.2226 62.5809H4.45164C3.59125 62.5809 2.89377 61.8834 2.89377 61.023V4.57204Z\" fill=\"white\"></path> <path d=\"M34.6774 18.3479H51.9922L33.1196 0.802246V16.79C33.1196 17.6504 33.8171 18.3479 34.6774 18.3479Z\" fill=\"#2172D0\"></path> <rect fill=\"#2172D0\" height=\"2.99978\" width=\"9.99928\" x=\"8.99524\" y=\"16.801\"></rect> <rect fill=\"#2172D0\" height=\"2.99978\" width=\"9.99928\" x=\"8.99524\" y=\"34.7998\"></rect> <rect fill=\"#2172D0\" height=\"2.99978\" width=\"23.9983\" x=\"8.99524\" y=\"25.8005\"></rect> <circle cx=\"44.9022\" cy=\"44.7086\" fill=\"white\" r=\"10.7622\" stroke=\"#2172D0\" stroke-width=\"2.47381\" transform=\"rotate(-49.859 44.9022 44.7086)\"></circle> <path d=\"M60.723 60.9036C61.7674 61.7844 63.3281 61.6517 64.2089 60.6073C65.0897 59.5628 64.957 58.0021 63.9126 57.1214L60.723 60.9036ZM52.2213 53.7341L60.723 60.9036L63.9126 57.1214L55.4109 49.9519L52.2213 53.7341Z\" fill=\"#2172D0\"></path> </svg> Application Instruction </a></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pct pct_mc\">\n<div class=\"pct pct_mc\">\n<div class=\"pct_st-tbc product-specification-table-small-padding\">\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\"></h2>\n<h2 class=\"pct_st\"></h2>\n<p> </p>\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\">Product Specifications</h2>\n<div class=\"pct_tbc\">\n<table class=\"pct_tb\" style=\"border-color: #adadad; font-weight: bold; height: 74px;\"><!-- 表头 -->\n<thead class=\"pct_th\">\n<tr style=\"height: 55px;\">\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"background-color: #c7c7c7; color: #333333; border-color: #adadad; font-weight: bold; text-align: center; height: 55px; width: 72.4574px;\">\n<div>Product ID</div>\n</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"background-color: #c7c7c7; color: #333333; border-color: #adadad; font-weight: bold; height: 55px; width: 148.139px;\">\n<div>Connector Model</div>\n</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"background-color: #c7c7c7; color: #333333; border-color: #adadad; font-weight: bold; height: 55px; width: 148.04px;\">\n<div>Maximum Current\n<div>\n<p>(A)</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"background-color: #c7c7c7; color: #333333; border-color: #adadad; font-weight: bold; height: 55px; width: 76.733px;\">\n<div>Maximum Voltage\n<div>\n<p>(V)</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"background-color: #c7c7c7; color: #333333; border-color: #adadad; font-weight: bold; height: 55px; width: 72.5284px;\">\n<div>Size</div>\n<p>(mm)</p>\n</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"background-color: #c7c7c7; color: #333333; border-color: #adadad; font-weight: bold; height: 55px; width: 72.5284px;\">\n<div>Weight</div>\n<p>(g)</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr class=\"pct_tr\" style=\"height: 19px;\">\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"border-color: #adadad; text-align: center; height: 19px; width: 72.4574px;\">IA007</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"border-color: #adadad; height: 19px; width: 148.139px;\">SH1.0-2P</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"border-color: #adadad; height: 19px; width: 148.04px;\">0.4A</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"border-color: #adadad; height: 19px; width: 76.733px;\">7.4V</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"border-color: #adadad; height: 19px; width: 72.5284px;\">39x15.5x20</td>\n<td class=\"pct_td\" style=\"border-color: #adadad; height: 19px; width: 72.5284px;\">3.5</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pct pct_mc\">\n<div class=\"pct_padding-in-mobile\">\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\"></h2>\n<h2 class=\"pct_st\"></h2>\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\">Introduction</h2>\n<h2 class=\"pct_st\"></h2>\n<p>Used with a Power Distribution Board (PDB) - 4 Channels, it is used to adjust the voltage of the corresponding channel, thereby achieving the function of adjusting the speed or brightness of the corresponding device.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>The Potentiometer Board with SH1.0 Connector is used for voltage regulation. It requires a Wire Pair with SH1.0 to connect to the SW0~4 channels on the Power Distribution Board (PDB) - 4 Channels. When the knob is turned counterclockwise, the output voltage of the corresponding channel decreases. When the knob is turned clockwise, the output voltage of the corresponding channel increases.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>If the Potentiometer Board is connected to any of the SW1~SW4 channels, ensure that the maximum current of the corresponding channel's device does not exceed 0.4A, and the battery voltage does not exceed 6V.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>If the Potentiometer Board is connected to the SW0 master switch, ensure that the combined maximum current of all channels SW1~SW4 does not exceed 0.4A, and the battery voltage does not exceed 6V.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>It is normal for the triode on the Potentiometer Board to heat up. When installing it on a model, please leave space for heat dissipation and avoid direct contact, which would cause the model material to heat up and soften.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n<!-- 图片 -->\n<div class=\"pct pct_mc\">\n<div class=\"pct_tpc-ic\">\n<div class=\"pct_ic\"><!-- 手机端图片 --> <img alt=\"Socket Head Cap Machine Screws (SHCS)\" class=\"pct_mi product-desc-lazy-media product-desc-lazy-media--image bg-bbl-white animate-pulse max-h-[400px]\" data-lazy=\"false\" data-src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0584/7236/6216/files/999.png?v=1718249904\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMjQiIGhlaWdodD0iMjQiIHZpZXdCb3g9IjAgMCAyNCAyNCIgZmlsbD0ibm9uZSIgeG1sbnM9Imh0dHA6Ly93d3cudzMub3JnLzIwMDAvc3ZnIj4KPHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjI0IiBoZWlnaHQ9IjI0IiBmaWxsPSIjRkZGRkZGIi8+Cjwvc3ZnPgo=\"/> <!-- PC端图片 --> <img alt=\"Socket Head Cap Machine Screws (SHCS)\" class=\"pct_i product-desc-lazy-media product-desc-lazy-media--image bg-bbl-white animate-pulse max-h-[400px]\" data-lazy=\"false\" data-src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0584/7236/6216/files/999.png?v=1718249904\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMjQiIGhlaWdodD0iMjQiIHZpZXdCb3g9IjAgMCAyNCAyNCIgZmlsbD0ibm9uZSIgeG1sbnM9Imh0dHA6Ly93d3cudzMub3JnLzIwMDAvc3ZnIj4KPHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjI0IiBoZWlnaHQ9IjI0IiBmaWxsPSIjRkZGRkZGIi8+Cjwvc3ZnPgo=\"/></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<!-- 图片结束 --><!-- table布局 --><!-- 物品清单布局结束 --><!-- 标题加文案 -->\n<div class=\"pct pct_mc\">\n<div class=\"pct_padding-in-mobile\">\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\"></h2>\n<p> </p>\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\">Electronics System</h2>\n<h2 class=\"pct_st\"></h2>\n<p>The components of this circuit set can be divided into five categories: <a href=\"../../../products/power-distribution-board-pdb-4-channels\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span><span style=\"color: #00ae42;\"><strong>Power Distribution Board (PDB) - 4 Channels</strong></span></span></a><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">,</span> power-type devices, power supply devices, switch devices, and wires. The Power Distribution Board has channels for connecting power supply devices, switch devices, and electric devices. Please refer to the figure below for the devices supported by each connector. The IN is used to connect various power supply devices, such as <a href=\"../../../products/battery-case-with-ph2-0-connector\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><span style=\"color: #00ae42;\"><strong>AA Battery Case</strong></span></span></a> and <a href=\"../../../products/usb-a-power-cable-with-ph2-0-connector\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><span style=\"color: #00ae42;\"><strong>USB-A Power Cable</strong></span></span></a>; the CH1-4 are used to connect various electric devices, such as <a href=\"../../../products/n20-reduction-gear-motor\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><span style=\"color: #00ae42;\"><strong>N20 Reduction Gear Motor (150rpm)</strong></span></span></a> and <a href=\"../../../products/3030-5v-led-board-with-sh1-0-connector\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><span style=\"color: #00ae42;\"><strong>4 White 3030-LED Board</strong></span></span></a>, and supports up to 4 connections; the SW0~4 is used to connect various switch devices, such as <a href=\"../../../products/self-locking-button-switch-with-sh1-0-connector\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><span style=\"color: #00ae42;\"><strong>Self-locking Button Switch</strong></span></span></a><a href=\"https://asia.store.bambulab.com/products/power-distribution-board-pdb-4-channelsbambulab.com/products/self-locking-button-switch-with-sh1-0-connector\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">, </a><a href=\"../../../products/potentiometer-board-with-sh1-0-connector\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #00ae42;\">Potentiometer Board</span></strong></span></a>, and <a href=\"../../../products/jumper-cable-with-sh1-0-connector\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><span style=\"color: #00ae42;\"><strong>Jumper Cable</strong></span></span></a>. Please do not connect electric devices to the SW0~4, and likewise, do not connect switches to the CH1~4. The OUT is used to connect to the next Power Distribution Board to achieve connector expansion. To learn more about case, please refer to the <a href=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0584/7236/6216/files/PDB_Potentiometer_Board_Self-Locking_Button_Switch-IA007.zip?v=1734419025\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color: #00ae42;\"><strong>Application Instruction</strong></span></a>.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pct pct_mc\">\n<div class=\"pct_padding-in-mobile\">\n<h2 class=\"pct_st\"></h2>\n<p> </p>\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\">In the box</h2>\n<h2 class=\"pct_st\"></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Potentiometer Board with SH1.0 Connector x2pcs</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Wire Pair with SH1.0 x2pcs</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pct pct_mc\">\n<div class=\"pct_padding-in-mobile\">\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\"></h2>\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\">Consideration</h2>\n<h2 class=\"pct_st\"></h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Please do not forcefully twist the connectors to avoid wires loosening or detaching.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>",
  "description_text": "Used with a Power Distribution Board (PDB) - 4 Channels, it is used to adjust the voltage of the corresponding channel, thereby achieving the function of adjusting the speed or brightness of the corresponding device.\n\nThe Potentiometer Board with SH1.0 Connector is used for voltage regulation. It requires a Wire Pair with SH1.0 to connect to the SW0~4 channels on the Power Distribution Board (PDB) - 4 Channels. When the knob is turned counterclockwise, the output voltage of the corresponding channel decreases. When the knob is turned clockwise, the output voltage of the corresponding channel increases.\n\nIf the Potentiometer Board is connected to any of the SW1~SW4 channels, ensure that the maximum current of the corresponding channel's device does not exceed 0.4A, and the battery voltage does not exceed 6V.\n\nIf the Potentiometer Board is connected to the SW0 master switch, ensure that the combined maximum current of all channels SW1~SW4 does not exceed 0.4A, and the battery voltage does not exceed 6V.\n\nIt is normal for the triode on the Potentiometer Board to heat up. When installing it on a model, please leave space for heat dissipation and avoid direct contact, which would cause the model material to heat up and soften.\n\nThe components of this circuit set can be divided into five categories: Power Distribution Board (PDB) - 4 Channels, power-type devices, power supply devices, switch devices, and wires. The Power Distribution Board has channels for connecting power supply devices, switch devices, and electric devices. Please refer to the figure below for the devices supported by each connector. The IN is used to connect various power supply devices, such as AA Battery Case and USB-A Power Cable; the CH1-4 are used to connect various electric devices, such as N20 Reduction Gear Motor (150rpm) and 4 White 3030-LED Board, and supports up to 4 connections; the SW0~4 is used to connect various switch devices, such as Self-locking Button Switch, Potentiometer Board, and Jumper Cable. Please do not connect electric devices to the SW0~4, and likewise, do not connect switches to the CH1~4. The OUT is used to connect to the next Power Distribution Board to achieve connector expansion. To learn more about case, please refer to the Application Instruction.\n\nPlease do not forcefully twist the connectors to avoid wires loosening or detaching.",
